  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adapting Public Investment to Climate Change in Latin America (IPACC II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between 11/2011 and 04/2015, in partnership with the Peruvian Ministries (MEF and MINAM), Adapting Public Investment to Climate Change Project (IPACC I)  was executed, achieving the implementation of climate risk analyses in the national procedures for public investment. Thereby, in order to exploit the Peruvian advances and expand their experiences, IPACC II was commissioned. On the one hand this project strengthened the capacities in Peru. On the other hand the innovative approach was adapted and transferred to other countries of Latin America, specifically to Brazil and Colombia. This project contributed considerably to reducing climate induced economic, social and ecologic damages and thereby led to a better adaptation to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
